{
  "schema": "sineforge.api-caller-workflow.v1",
  "id": "d85a8acf-4310-5c4d-b503-b57343bad0bd",
  "name": "4. Qwen3-TTS VoiceClone + SaveVoice",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "4. Qwen3-TTS VoiceClone + SaveVoice is a speech & voice workflow designed to synthesize, design, clone, save, or reuse a speaking voice using Qwen3-TTS. Its 8-node graph exposes 2 prompt/text field(s), 1 media input target(s), and 2 save/preview stage(s), while preserving the original editor-format graph for reference. The imported graph contains unresolved custom-node classes, so install or map the listed nodes and reconvert from the included editor graph before production use.",
  "category": "Speech, Audio & Music",
  "subcategory": "Speech & voice",
  "episode": "EP07",
  "instructions": "1. Install or map the unresolved node classes listed in Requirements, open the included editor-format source in the main LTX ComfyUI install, and export API format again before attempting a run.\n2. Confirm that any model selectors in the editable inputs resolve to files available in the main ComfyUI installation.\n3. Upload and assign the required image, mask, video, or audio files to the listed media inputs. Keep the source dimensions and duration appropriate for the selected model.\n4. Review text, speaker/voice references, language, duration, sample rate, and seed. For cloning, use a clean reference clip and confirm you have permission to use the voice.\n5. Save a copy before making structural changes. Use Editable inputs for normal parameters and Raw API JSON only when you need to inspect or change graph wiring.\n6. Validate again after every change. Queue one workflow only after validation passes; then inspect the returned output, logs, duration, dimensions, and media integrity.",
  "tags": [
    "EP07",
    "Qwen3-TTS",
    "Speech & voice",
    "Speech, Audio & Music"
  ],
