    "prompt_field_count": 2,
    "output_node_count": 2,
    "documentation_notes": "Hi, I’m using a woman’s voice to talk to you right now. It’s smooth, it’s clear and it sounds pretty natural. Kinda cool, right?\n\nWelcome to Pixaroma Radio. This is Alison speaking. Today we’re testing a cloned female voice inside ComfyUI. Pretty cool, right?\n\n# MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW  \n\n---\n\n### Models are downloaded automatically the first time you use the workflow.\n \n---\n\n## 🧩 Nodes Installed from Manager  \n\n- ComfyUI-Easy-Use\n- Qwen3-TTS - Voice Synthesis & Cloning\n- ComfyUI_LayerStyle\n\nRead More about Qwen TTS Node [HERE](https://github.com/flybirdxx/ComfyUI-Qwen-TTS)\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources  \n🎥 **Tutorials:** [Pixaroma YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma)  \n💬 **Community Discord:** [Join Here](https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3)\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Qwen3 Voice Clone + Save Voice Workflow\n\n### What it does\n- Clones a voice from a **10–20s voice sample**\n- Generates speech from **Speech Text** in that cloned voice\n- Saves the cloned voice as a reusable preset (**SaveVoice**)\n- Saves an MP3 of the generated audio\n\n### How to use\n1. **Load Voice Sample (10–20s)**: load your reference voice audio (one speaker, clean, no music).\n2. **Reference Audio Text**: type the exact words spoken in the voice sample (must match).\n3. **Speech Text**: type what you want the cloned voice to say.\n4. Set **filename** in **SaveVoice** (example: `my_custom_voice`).\n5. Click **Run**\n\n### Save locations\n- MP3 preview is in **Save Audio (MP3)**\n- MP3 saves under: **ComfyUI\\\\output\\\\audio** \n- Saved voices (SaveVoice) are stored in: **ComfyUI\\\\models\\\\qwen-tts\\\\voices**"
  },
